WEBVTT

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:01.930
<i>Twenty-five years ago,</i>

00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:08.510
<i>massive creatures called Dragons 
emerged into the world.</i>

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:12.400
Why is there a man here?

00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:15.450
The first male student since 
the academy was founded.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:17.760
Mononobe Yuu.

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:20.810
It's been three years,

00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:23.300
Nii-san.

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:32.800
Reconnection: accepted.

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:36.950
Seeking: destruction.

00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:39.180
Of all other Dragonkind.

00:00:39.490 --> 00:00:41.680
I'm a Dragon!

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:45.230
You're a cute human girl.

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:50.200
Now, get rid of everything false.

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:52.530
Become your true self.

00:00:57.870 --> 00:00:59.740
Lisa! Lisa!

00:01:00.050 --> 00:01:00.950
Let go of Tear,

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:05.290
Kili Surtr Muspelheim.

00:01:08.570 --> 00:01:10.220
I won't go.

00:01:10.220 --> 00:01:12.100
I'm staying here.

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:16.840
Besides, I'm going to become Yuu's bride!

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:21.140
I'm a human girl!

00:01:29.150 --> 00:01:30.560
Mitsuki-chan!

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:36.990
So what'll it be?

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:59.050
<b><i>Unlimited Fafnir</i></b>

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:11.370
<b>Scarlet Innocent</b>

00:03:08.390 --> 00:03:09.610
Kili!

00:03:09.610 --> 00:03:11.790
Just what are you?

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:14.290
I'm a Dragon.

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:17.760
You don't intend to answer, do you?

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:22.000
I'm not avoiding your question or anything.

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:24.900
But if you don't mind,

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:26.720
maybe you can decide for me.

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:32.660
Let's meet again.

00:03:32.660 --> 00:03:34.900
Do the best you can.

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:49.170
Respond, please, Shinomiya-sensei.

00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:50.290
Principal!

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:52.320
Please respond!

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:55.460
Shinomiya-sensei...

00:03:55.990 --> 00:03:57.360
Mononobe.

00:03:57.360 --> 00:03:58.420
Tear-chan.

00:04:00.170 --> 00:04:02.660
Lisa's not responding, either.

00:04:09.570 --> 00:04:10.510
<i>Mitsuki.</i>

00:04:10.510 --> 00:04:11.900
<i>Can you hear me, Mitsuki?</i>

00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:13.100
Nii-san.

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:14.730
Mononobe!

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:22.680
Good thing it's slow-moving.

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:24.660
Mitsuki, I need directions.

00:04:25.230 --> 00:04:28.250
Lend us your anti-Dragon equipment.

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:33.830
We're going to force the 
Hecatoncheir out of the academy.

00:04:33.830 --> 00:04:35.150
How?

00:04:36.190 --> 00:04:38.040
Neither heat nor lasers work.

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:39.430
<i>Neither heat nor lasers work.</i>

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:42.240
Wind.

00:04:42.750 --> 00:04:43.340
Wind?

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:45.930
<i>We'll generate as much wind as we can,</i>

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:47.780
<i>and smash it against the Hecatoncheir.</i>

00:04:48.870 --> 00:04:50.410
<i>Once it's in the water,</i>

00:04:50.410 --> 00:04:53.270
<i>we should be able to make a large-scale attack.</i>

00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:56.230
Sounds like it's worth a try.

00:04:56.580 --> 00:04:58.940
All right, let's do it.

00:05:00.340 --> 00:05:03.390
I'll meet up with you once I evacuate Tear.

00:05:06.220 --> 00:05:07.060
Tear?

00:05:09.950 --> 00:05:10.970
I'm...

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:13.410
I'm fighting, too.

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:16.710
<i>Y-You can't, Tear-chan.</i>

00:05:17.110 --> 00:05:20.530
It might be after you.

00:05:20.530 --> 00:05:21.960
You have to hide.

00:05:22.510 --> 00:05:23.670
No,

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:25.790
I'm not running anymore.

00:05:27.970 --> 00:05:30.140
I'm fighting with the rest of you.

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:31.580
Tear.

00:05:33.490 --> 00:05:36.970
What if you go berserk, 
like you did during training?

00:05:37.420 --> 00:05:38.310
It'll be fine.

00:05:39.140 --> 00:05:41.520
I'm not a Dragon anymore.

00:05:43.630 --> 00:05:44.660
All right.

00:05:45.150 --> 00:05:46.490
Let's fight together.

00:05:47.590 --> 00:05:48.910
Thanks.

00:05:49.340 --> 00:05:50.160
Is that all right,

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:51.210
<i>Mitsuki?</i>

00:05:52.060 --> 00:05:52.960
I understand.

00:05:52.960 --> 00:05:54.250
Mitsuki-chan.

00:05:54.740 --> 00:05:58.750
The desire to protect is often a great power.

00:05:59.460 --> 00:06:01.720
<i>Isn't that right, Nii-san?</i>

00:06:01.720 --> 00:06:02.540
Yeah.

00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:29.320
It appears the Hecatoncheir 
has found Tear-san.

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:34.280
Let's time our air conversions to maximize them.

00:06:34.690 --> 00:06:38.280
Aim for the abdomen, 
where its center of gravity is.

00:06:38.280 --> 00:06:42.710
Countdown: Five, four, three...

00:06:53.740 --> 00:06:54.690
Fire!

00:06:54.690 --> 00:06:57.380
First arrow: Folk Wind!

00:06:59.690 --> 00:07:01.480
Aero Blast Quartet!

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:06.640
Generate Windstorm!

00:07:08.660 --> 00:07:09.760
Go!

00:07:11.890 --> 00:07:15.280
Storm Winds! Hit it!

00:07:26.480 --> 00:07:27.680
It fell over!

00:07:28.140 --> 00:07:29.380
It's too heavy.

00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:31.840
Move to Formation B.

00:07:35.850 --> 00:07:37.930
<i>My power.</i>

00:07:37.930 --> 00:07:40.020
<i>My greatest power.</i>

00:07:40.540 --> 00:07:42.270
<i>My greatest...</i>

00:07:49.040 --> 00:07:52.060
Go!

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:15.400
<i>It's no good.</i>

00:08:15.400 --> 00:08:17.290
<i>We have to push it further away.</i>

00:08:20.480 --> 00:08:24.320
Noin. Request: confirmed.

00:08:27.120 --> 00:08:28.410
Yggdrasil.

00:08:28.410 --> 00:08:34.910
All powers transferred at time 
of Fear and Leviathan's defeat.

00:08:35.640 --> 00:08:39.470
Activation request: Code Fear.

00:08:40.470 --> 00:08:44.170
Activation request: Anti-gravity.

00:08:47.510 --> 00:08:49.280
Anti-gravity!

00:09:07.420 --> 00:09:09.840
Is that a repulsion field?

00:09:11.640 --> 00:09:13.490
Now! Once more!

00:09:13.840 --> 00:09:15.950
Everyone, prepare to attack!

00:09:18.290 --> 00:09:20.620
Fire in fifteen counts.

00:09:20.920 --> 00:09:23.080
Fifteen, fourteen...

00:09:24.750 --> 00:09:26.370
Lend me your strength.

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:28.580
We're going to blow it away.

00:09:30.340 --> 00:09:31.200
Okay.

00:09:31.200 --> 00:09:33.090
I'm your wife.

00:09:33.290 --> 00:09:35.550
I'm going to work hard with my husband.

00:09:38.900 --> 00:09:41.810
Seeking: destruction.

00:09:42.780 --> 00:09:48.150
The information you possess 
on the Marduke is incomplete.

00:09:48.700 --> 00:09:51.290
Recommending additional downloads.

00:09:51.990 --> 00:09:55.240
Compensation: your memories.

00:09:55.630 --> 00:09:56.700
<i>I don't need that.</i>

00:09:57.550 --> 00:09:58.820
<i>Three years ago,</i>

00:09:58.820 --> 00:10:00.960
<i>I fought off a Hecatoncheir</i>

00:10:00.960 --> 00:10:02.910
<i>when the Marduke was even more incomplete.</i>

00:10:03.940 --> 00:10:05.070
<i>Besides...</i>

00:10:11.010 --> 00:10:13.000
<i>I don't want to lose any more</i>

00:10:13.940 --> 00:10:17.350
<i>of my precious memories and feelings!</i>

00:10:23.910 --> 00:10:26.020
...two, one!

00:10:26.880 --> 00:10:27.890
Fire!

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:36.360
Windstorm!

00:10:58.300 --> 00:11:00.590
Special artillery Megiddo!

00:11:01.200 --> 00:11:02.280
Fire!

00:11:56.800 --> 00:11:58.650
No signs of regeneration.

00:11:59.120 --> 00:12:01.120
We've defeated it!

00:12:03.370 --> 00:12:04.560
We did it.

00:12:04.560 --> 00:12:06.870
Tear-chan, we won!

00:12:08.230 --> 00:12:09.150
Yeah.

00:12:10.460 --> 00:12:11.330
Yeah!

00:12:11.600 --> 00:12:13.280
We did it, Tear-chan!

00:12:13.280 --> 00:12:15.130
We did it!

00:12:15.720 --> 00:12:16.540
We did it!

00:12:18.560 --> 00:12:19.500
Nii-san.

00:12:19.890 --> 00:12:20.630
Yeah.

00:12:21.520 --> 00:12:22.880
<i>I'm fine.</i>

00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:24.480
<i>I haven't changed.</i>

00:12:32.240 --> 00:12:34.900
Damn, that was seriously rough.

00:12:37.110 --> 00:12:39.590
My... My room!

00:12:40.150 --> 00:12:42.470
My treasure collection!

00:12:43.160 --> 00:12:48.240
You won't get away with this, you blue bastard!

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:51.400
You're really getting it if you regenerate again!

00:12:51.400 --> 00:12:54.750
I'll grab you like this, then do this, and...

00:12:54.750 --> 00:12:59.210
That's why I was against you 
building your room so high up.

00:12:59.800 --> 00:13:04.980
You know what they say about fools 
and smoke loving high places.

00:13:04.980 --> 00:13:08.530
You could learn a little from Shinomiya.

00:13:13.310 --> 00:13:15.230
It's safe now, everyone.

00:13:15.840 --> 00:13:17.150
Okay.

00:13:31.510 --> 00:13:32.640
Lisa.

00:13:34.200 --> 00:13:36.760
Tear-san.

00:13:38.760 --> 00:13:40.030
Lisa!

00:13:40.030 --> 00:13:41.460
Thank goodness!

00:13:41.910 --> 00:13:43.580
Lisa...

00:13:43.580 --> 00:13:45.530
Thank you.

00:13:49.600 --> 00:13:51.150
Sorry.

00:13:52.030 --> 00:13:54.310
I want to pat your head,

00:13:55.440 --> 00:13:56.830
but I can't.

00:13:57.200 --> 00:13:59.920
No. No.

00:14:00.590 --> 00:14:02.800
You protected me.

00:14:02.800 --> 00:14:05.760
Thank you, Lisa.

00:14:07.900 --> 00:14:11.600
Really, though, you made a huge mess.

00:14:11.600 --> 00:14:15.700
We fought with the 
Hecatoncheir and with Kili.

00:14:15.700 --> 00:14:19.050
We should be glad that it wasn't worse.

00:14:19.630 --> 00:14:21.680
And there's still the Basilisk.

00:14:21.680 --> 00:14:24.340
We'll have to think about 
our plans going forward.

00:14:24.740 --> 00:14:28.800
Mononobe Mitsuki, you must be 
troubled by the loss of your room.

00:14:29.230 --> 00:14:31.630
You can use the other housing for a while.

00:14:32.030 --> 00:14:34.310
Yes, Shinomiya-sensei.

00:14:36.620 --> 00:14:39.130
The roof and bed are both burned up.

00:14:39.730 --> 00:14:41.310
What are you going to do, Mononobe?

00:14:41.570 --> 00:14:43.100
I wonder.

00:14:43.100 --> 00:14:45.960
If it's okay with you,

00:14:47.560 --> 00:14:52.200
h-how about my room?

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:54.980
We can get married if you need a room.

00:14:55.590 --> 00:14:56.420
Wait a second.

00:14:56.420 --> 00:15:00.400
'Cause you can live in my 
room once we're married.

00:15:00.400 --> 00:15:03.420
Again, why are we getting 
married all of a sudden?

00:15:03.980 --> 00:15:05.860
It's not sudden.

00:15:05.860 --> 00:15:10.550
I've always said I'm going to be your wife.

00:15:11.580 --> 00:15:13.640
Do you not want to?

00:15:14.160 --> 00:15:16.770
It's not about whether I want to or not.

00:15:16.770 --> 00:15:18.480
I told you before.

00:15:18.480 --> 00:15:20.200
According to human rules,

00:15:20.200 --> 00:15:22.960
we aren't old enough to get married.

00:15:22.960 --> 00:15:25.230
Th-That's right, Tear-chan.

00:15:26.180 --> 00:15:28.780
Then let's get engaged for now.

00:15:34.640 --> 00:15:37.120
Now we're engaged!

00:15:37.710 --> 00:15:40.300
That's not fair, Tear-chan!

00:15:40.300 --> 00:15:41.580
I can do that, too.

00:15:41.860 --> 00:15:43.080
Nope.

00:15:43.080 --> 00:15:45.040
We already kissed, so we're engaged.

00:15:45.450 --> 00:15:47.510
Just on the cheek, 
because it's an engagement.

00:15:47.510 --> 00:15:49.490
And then when we get married,

00:15:49.490 --> 00:15:51.010
I'll kiss him on the mouth.

00:15:51.280 --> 00:15:54.340
I k-kissed him already, too.

00:15:55.630 --> 00:15:57.020
You're lying.

00:15:58.110 --> 00:15:59.210
Mitsuki.

00:16:00.910 --> 00:16:05.060
You'll be in the room next to mine, 
in the common housing.

00:16:05.990 --> 00:16:06.960
Right.

00:16:08.010 --> 00:16:10.480
Why are you making so much 
noise in the classroom?

00:16:10.480 --> 00:16:12.530
Keeping quiet is a basic rule in any school.

00:16:13.170 --> 00:16:15.270
Sorry, Mitsuki-chan.

00:16:15.270 --> 00:16:17.170
Sorry.

00:16:20.810 --> 00:16:22.830
Nii-san is most at fault.

00:16:39.490 --> 00:16:41.180
What are you so angry about?

00:16:41.580 --> 00:16:44.830
I'm in the middle of writing a 
report on what just happened.

00:16:44.830 --> 00:16:46.540
Please don't talk to me.

00:16:52.080 --> 00:16:54.110
So you are angry.

00:16:57.260 --> 00:16:58.800
I need to talk to you.

00:16:58.800 --> 00:16:59.780
S-Sure.

00:17:00.460 --> 00:17:03.470
First, about the Hecatoncheir.

00:17:03.470 --> 00:17:05.680
Why did it show up all of a sudden?

00:17:07.170 --> 00:17:09.520
It disappeared from Siberia,

00:17:09.520 --> 00:17:15.010
where it was contained at the 
moment it appeared at Midgar.

00:17:16.120 --> 00:17:19.220
Does that mean it warped here?

00:17:19.840 --> 00:17:21.040
I don't know.

00:17:21.560 --> 00:17:26.220
There haven't been any reports 
of such an ability until now.

00:17:27.710 --> 00:17:29.690
More importantly,

00:17:30.080 --> 00:17:34.620
what was that Leviathan-like power

00:17:34.620 --> 00:17:38.230
that canceled out gravity for a moment?

00:17:48.780 --> 00:17:53.650
Well, I just kinda thought I'd give it a try,

00:17:53.650 --> 00:17:55.720
and it worked.

00:17:56.040 --> 00:17:59.500
We can't have you "just trying" 
to make something like that.

00:18:02.270 --> 00:18:05.930
Don't you think you're 
keeping too many secrets?

00:18:12.020 --> 00:18:13.860
We still have our home.

00:18:15.060 --> 00:18:20.280
That city is where my family can belong.

00:18:21.620 --> 00:18:23.510
I'm not giving up.

00:18:23.510 --> 00:18:27.130
Not against that thing that took 
all the people I love away.

00:18:27.130 --> 00:18:29.250
I'm not letting it have me, too.

00:18:33.160 --> 00:18:34.710
<i>I wanted strength.</i>

00:18:35.500 --> 00:18:38.710
Seeking: destruction.

00:18:39.630 --> 00:18:43.280
Compensation: your memories.

00:18:50.760 --> 00:18:54.400
You insist on keeping your secrets, then.

00:18:54.400 --> 00:18:56.170
No, like I said—

00:18:56.170 --> 00:18:57.310
Then...

00:18:59.040 --> 00:19:02.640
Please answer my next question.

00:19:04.890 --> 00:19:05.810
Nii-san,

00:19:07.040 --> 00:19:11.170
is it true that you kissed Iris-san?

00:19:18.650 --> 00:19:24.050
That was to thank her for when 
we fought against the Leviathan.

00:19:25.020 --> 00:19:28.170
So you really did.

00:19:29.840 --> 00:19:30.560
Yes.

00:19:31.920 --> 00:19:33.290
I see.

00:19:47.080 --> 00:19:50.950
Please deal with it, with integrity.

00:19:51.860 --> 00:19:55.680
Otherwise I'll deem it to 
be an act of indecency.

00:19:57.540 --> 00:19:58.340
Right.

00:19:59.220 --> 00:20:00.170
Got it.

00:20:01.100 --> 00:20:02.000
But...

00:20:05.420 --> 00:20:09.660
I have to apologize, too.

00:20:10.980 --> 00:20:13.390
To you and Iris-san.

00:20:14.390 --> 00:20:15.480
Why?

00:20:15.840 --> 00:20:17.170
Why?

00:20:17.900 --> 00:20:18.960
Because...

00:20:21.300 --> 00:20:24.160
I'm sure it was the first time for Iris-san.

00:20:25.760 --> 00:20:27.200
But your first was...

00:20:28.310 --> 00:20:31.160
with me.

00:20:33.760 --> 00:20:35.220
<i>I don't remember.</i>

00:20:37.790 --> 00:20:41.280
I-It's the same as with Tear-san.

00:20:41.280 --> 00:20:43.050
It was something we did as kids.

00:20:44.240 --> 00:20:46.770
The kiss, the promise...

00:20:47.300 --> 00:20:49.780
Pretend none of it ever happened.

00:20:49.780 --> 00:20:51.470
I would appreciate it.

00:20:52.810 --> 00:20:54.020
Mitsuki...

00:20:54.560 --> 00:20:56.950
Don't say the memories we 
shared never happened.

00:20:56.950 --> 00:20:58.180
Not even as a joke.

00:21:02.830 --> 00:21:06.370
You're always kind, aren't you, Nii-san?

00:21:07.190 --> 00:21:11.700
But I can't be so nice to myself.

00:21:12.780 --> 00:21:14.950
I'm going to continue fighting the Dragons

00:21:15.580 --> 00:21:17.760
to atone for my crimes.

00:21:19.480 --> 00:21:21.710
I don't need my childhood wishes

00:21:22.830 --> 00:21:24.720
to come true.

00:21:30.360 --> 00:21:32.850
Nii-san...

00:21:33.530 --> 00:21:38.020
If you can only accept who you are 
by putting yourself in battle,

00:21:39.480 --> 00:21:42.860
then I'll end that battle.

00:21:43.720 --> 00:21:45.550
Listen, Mitsuki.

00:21:46.240 --> 00:21:50.070
I'll never give up on your happiness.

00:21:59.260 --> 00:22:00.500
Seriously.

00:22:01.160 --> 00:22:03.460
You're so

00:22:04.540 --> 00:22:08.600
stubborn, Nii-san.

00:23:39.810 --> 00:24:09.670
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:40.720 --> 00:23:41.730
We did it!

00:23:41.730 --> 00:23:43.230
We defeated the Hecatoncheir,

00:23:43.230 --> 00:23:47.320
but now the Basilisk is attacking?

00:23:47.320 --> 00:23:48.560
We have no choice, then.

00:23:48.560 --> 00:23:50.260
Let's go defeat it.

00:23:50.260 --> 00:23:52.890
I'm excited about going by boat.

00:23:52.890 --> 00:23:55.740
What? Mitsuki and Lisa are fighting?

00:23:56.530 --> 00:23:59.250
I don't think I can do anything about that.

00:23:59.840 --> 00:24:04.630
Next time on <i>Unlimited Fafnir</i>: 
"Basilisk Attacks."

00:24:04.630 --> 00:24:07.720
Mononobe-kun, if it's really bothering you,

00:24:07.720 --> 00:24:09.670
you should ask Fyril.

00:24:09.670 --> 00:24:19.920
<b>Illustration: Saburouta</b>
